data.content:
## What Changed

.NET 10's `Microsoft.AspNetCore.OpenApi` upgraded to **Microsoft.OpenApi v2**, which has several breaking changes:

| .NET 9 (OpenApi v1) | .NET 10 (OpenApi v2) |
|---|---|
| `Microsoft.OpenApi.Any.*` types (`OpenApiString`, etc.) | Removed — use `System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode` |
| `schema.Example = new OpenApiString(...)` | `schema.Example = JsonValue.Create(...)` |
| `schema.Nullable = true/false` | Removed — nullability via `JsonSchemaType` flags |
| `OpenApiSecurityRequirement` is a `Dictionary<>` | Has a `Schemes` property instead |
| `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` | Renamed to `ReferenceType.SecurityScheme` still exists but `OpenApiReference` constructor changed |

## Fixed Code

```csharp
using System.Text.Json.Nodes;        // replaces Microsoft.OpenApi.Any
using Microsoft.OpenApi.Models;

options.AddOperationTransformer((operation, context, ct) =>
{
    var param = operation.Parameters.FirstOrDefault(p => p.Name == "api-version");
    if (param is not null)
    {
        // OpenApiString is gone; use JsonNode instead
        param.Schema.Example = JsonValue.Create("1.0");
    }

    operation.Responses.TryAdd("401", new OpenApiResponse { Description = "Unauthorized" });

    var oAuthScheme = new OpenApiSecurityScheme
    {
        Reference = new OpenApiReference { Type = ReferenceType.SecurityScheme, Id = "oauth2" }
    };

    // OpenApiSecurityRequirement is no longer a Dictionary itself;
    // use its Schemes property instead
    operation.Security = new List<OpenApiSecurityRequirement>
    {
        new OpenApiSecurityRequirement
        {
            Schemes = new Dictionary<OpenApiSecurityScheme, IList<string>>
            {
                [oAuthScheme] = scopes
            }
        }
    };

    return Task.CompletedTask;
});

options.AddSchemaTransformer((schema, context, ct) =>
{
    if (schema.Properties is not null)
    {
        foreach (var property in schema.Properties)
        {
            if (schema.Required?.Contains(property.Key) != true)
            {
                // Nullable property is removed; clear the Null flag from Type
                property.Value.Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null;
            }
        }
    }
    return Task.CompletedTask;
});
```

## Summary of Fixes

1. **`OpenApiString` → `JsonValue.Create()`** — Replace `using Microsoft.OpenApi.Any` with `using System.Text.Json.Nodes`.
2. **`Nullable = false` → `Type &= ~JsonSchemaType.Null`** — Nullability is now a flag in the `Type` enum.
3. **`OpenApiSecurityRequirement { [scheme] = scopes }` → set the `.Schemes` dictionary** — It's no longer a dictionary subclass.
